From 6ad43301d07dfa9c31f3d6d5d22dd0d549696df3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Navi48-MacOS contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] radv: Darwin (macOS) backend with canned gfx1201 device
 info (Navi48 S1a)

Build RADV for Darwin without libdrm and without a DRM node.  meson: allow
-Dvulkan-drivers=amd on Darwin (no libdrm_amdgpu; compile vk_drm_syncobj.c;
HAVE_TSERVER for addrlib; -undefined dynamic_lookup like KosmicKrisp).
ac_linux_drm.c dispatches to a new Darwin backend (src/amd/common/darwin):
device info is the drm-shim gfx1201 table, the VA manager is libdrm's
(vendored), syncobjs are a userspace util_sync_provider, and every kernel
call returns -ENODEV with a log line (S1b/c wire them to the kext).
RADV enumerates the one device through vk_instance's .enumerate hook, only
when RADV_DARWIN_FAKE=1.  RADV_DARWIN_HOST_BO=1 makes BOs host memory so
vkCreateDevice succeeds; the first real stub then is CS submit.
Stand-in headers for xf86drm.h, amdgpu.h (libdrm's, verbatim) and libsync.h
live in include/darwin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
